Widescreen ranges: ask the camera what the extra columns show.

Reported after 0051: the side-on ranges helped, artifacts remain. Every
node-count rule (k, the side-on reach, the side-on window) guesses where the
camera looks; forward paths, most of the game, still had k = 2. The camera
itself is readable:

- rotation 0x80060774, loaded into the GTE by 0x8004EF28 just before the
  world draw (the renderer only clears the translation, 0x80041E9C);
- position 0x800607F4 (24.8, world units); each frame every world record of
  the zone header gets origin - camera, +16 the world's info, +20 triangles,
  +24 quads, +28 vertices (0x80018344..0x800183CC);
- world geometry: vertices' XY words last-first then Z halves, triangles a
  word each last-first then a half each, quads 8 bytes; coordinate = field &
  0xFFF0 from the origin (the renderer, 0x80041FBC..0x80042220). All 1.57M
  polygon references of the side-on paths decode.

crash2_wide_geom.h: the camera from the GTE, the RTPS projection in integers
(no translation, no squash), classification of a polygon against the 4:3 and
the wide frame, the current zone's worlds and polygon corners. 32 more code
words checked.

crash2_wide_slst.h: per node, candidates = what the lists within 20 nodes
(and the linked paths') hold that the game's list does not; each frame, the
ones reaching into the extra columns (outside 4:3, inside the wide frame, in
front) are drawn, nearest first, after their anchors. Nothing is added inside
the 4:3 frame - the game's list there is authoritative. Once per node the
model must put at least half of the game's own list on screen, else the
node window (0051) draws.

crash2_wide_spawn.h: with that camera, an object the original has not
spawned (or just killed) is wanted while its position projects into the
extra columns, on any path; load/unload rules unchanged. Camera y is read
signed: the game shifts it unsigned (harmless for its 16-bit offsets), but
it is negative in some levels.

Counters: wide_slst camera / model_bad / model_pct, wide_spawn cam_yes /
cam_no. tuning/wide_frustum_sim checks it on 72 real cases against a
separately written reference. No file here is in codegen_hash_sources.cmake;
overlay shards are unaffected.

